{
  "id": "ss.relic.mason",
  "name": "Mason gland",
  "description": "Three blocks of chewed earth stood up in an arc, the middle one tallest and set back, the outer two shorter and turned slightly outward — the cover the relic raises, with the gaps between them left wide on purpose, because never walling its owner in is half of what the relic does. Each block is a squared prism: a dark left facet and a foreshortened top face, deliberately not an elliptical cap, which read as a barrel in two earlier passes. The middle one has a wet run down it — the material is secreted mortar, not cut stone, and cut stone is the one vocabulary the ruins' own pillars and slabs already own. The gland itself is not drawn: a sac would have read as one more of the glands already on this shelf, and the arc is the only part of this that says what it does.",
